  "artist": {
    "name": "Amy Keane",
    "bio": "I am a representational painter, urban and nature sketcher living in Austin, Texas with my family. I\u2019ve studied and practiced art throughout my life, and became a full time artist in 2023. \n\nI focus on impressionistically painting flowers, still lifes and landscapes, mainly in acrylic or gouache paint. I like broad strokes and a loose feel in my paintings. I also like using a limited palette of colors to help create unity.  I also keep a sketch journal filled with pen and ink and watercolors. \n\nIn the scenes I paint, I hope to convey a story or sense of place that will make the viewer feel relaxed and visually intrigued.  ",
